    "content": "To access your Western Digital My Cloud, log in at MyCloud.com or use the My Cloud desktop/mobile apps with your credentials. Alternatively, access it locally via Windows File Explorer or macOS Finder under the \"Network\" section. For Apple iCloud, visit iCloud.com in a browser. MyCloud.com My Cloud desktop/mobile apps iCloud.com Accessing WD My Cloud (Network Attached Storage) Web Portal: Go to MyCloud.com and sign in to view files via a web browser. MyCloud.com Desktop App: Install the My Cloud desktop app to access files directly from your computer. Local Network (Windows): Open File Explorer, click \"Network,\" and double-click your My Cloud device. Local Network (macOS): Open Finder, check the shared section, and connect. Direct USB Connect: For some models, connect via USB and browse in File Explorer. Accessing Apple iCloud Web Browser: Go to iCloud.com to access files, photos, and apps from any computer. iCloud.com Apple Devices: Use the native Files app on iOS or Finder on macOS. Troubleshooting Connection IssuesIf the device is not appearing, ensure it is connected to the same network and that the LED light is solid blue, indicating it is active.",
